Incredibly realistic simulator!
You can discover many ways of breaking a car in this game.
For instance:
overheat the clutch when letting it slip for a while;
Break gears in the gearbox when shifting without clutch;
Blow your engine by activating an overkill nitrous tank in the car;
Crash into a tree and see how the car folds around it;
rolling over the Pigeon when "making a steering at the high speeds";
overheat the engine when sleeping on the gas pedal;
overheat the brakes and crash into a traffic light at insane speeds;
spawn 4 cars and set the AI to "chase me";
hit a small speed bump at 300km/h.
Not only is this game about wrecking and torturing cars, it's also about relaxing trips on the highway, mountain roads and extreme racing. Car handling is super realistic. Grip, engine torque, heat simulation, brake force and air resistance are calculated at real-life level. For instance, When you take a right corner at 50km/h with the left-front tire blown you will have understeer, and a car that has a spoiler on the back and front will have better grip in corners but will be slower at high speeds in comparison to the same car without spoilers.
You can finetune every car in the game by adjusting suspension strength, gear ratios, fuel tank volume, spoiler wing angles and many more things.
Other than that, the mod support is just awesome. There is an in-game mod repository so you don't have to open your browser and download mods manually.
The game is now singleplayer only, with a multiseat option. I don't think there will be multiplayer soon since it is very difficult to create. However, the game is more than enjoyable!
Controller support is really well done, it can see 2 different keyboards or controllers apart from eacht other, which is a feature i proudly made use of:
I have 2 steering wheels including pedals lying around, both of them have 2 pedals used for gas and braking. I'm using 1 set for steering, gas and brake, and the 2nd set for clutch and a free-to-assign pedal. This way I don't have to buy a new steering set with 3 pedals on it :D
The game is well optimized and it gets better every update.
My Specs:
CPU: Intel Pentium G4600 @3.5GHz
GPU: GTX 1050Ti
RAM: 8GB DDR4 @2400MHz
I can run the game at normal-high at 60fps and above on big maps.
Only on huge, I mean REALLY HUGE maps like Tennessee Road (mod) it sometimes drops to 40.

